## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourname/loremaster.git
cd loremaster
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate      # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Make sure Ollama is running and your model is pulled:

```bash
ollama pull llama3.1           # TODO: your model
ollama serve                   # if not already running as a service
```

## Configuration

Copy the example config and point it at your vault:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# then edit .env
```

| Variable        | Description                                   | Required |
|-----------------|-----------------------------------------------|----------|
| `VAULT_PATH`    | Path to your Obsidian vault / notes folder    | Yes      |
| `OLLAMA_MODEL`  | Model name to use (e.g. `llama3.1`)           | Yes      |
| `OLLAMA_HOST`   | Ollama endpoint (default `http://localhost:11434`) | No  |
| `EMBED_MODEL`   | Embedding model for indexing notes            | No       |

